{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"location","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLCancelV8LocationO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel\/Location-swift.enum"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"location"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel\/location-swift.property","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"location","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLCancelV8LocationO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"location","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLCancelV8locationAC8LocationOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcancel\/location-swift.property"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the cancellation appears relative to the new key signature."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLCancel/Location-swift.enum":{"abstract":[{"text":"The cancel-location type is used to indicate where a key signature cancellation appears relative to a new key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signature: to the left, to the right, or before the barline and to the left. It is left by default. For mid-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measure key elements, a cancel-location of before-barline should be treated like a cancel-location of left.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLCancel.Location","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Location","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcancel\/location-swift.enum","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel\/Location-swift.enum"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLCancel/location-swift.property":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the cancellation appears relative to the new key signature."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcancel\/location-swift.property","kind":"symbol","title":"location","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel\/location-swift.property","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"location","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLCancelV8LocationO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLCancel":{"title":"MXLCancel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLCancel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcancel","abstract":[{"text":"A cancel element indicates that the old key signature should be canceled before the new one appears. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"will always happen when changing to C major or A minor and need not be specified then. The cancel value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches the fifths value of the canceled key signature (e.g., a cancel of -2 will provide an explicit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation for changing from B flat major to F major). The optional location attribute indicates where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation appears relative to the new key signature.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCancel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLCancel","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}